{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this admission. You’re here for your next dose of high-dose methotrexate for your lymphoma. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’m okay, a bit tired, but no major pain. I’m just hoping this round goes better than the last one—I had really bad mouth sores."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. That was from the higher dose. This time we’re using 3500 mg/m², which is lower and should be easier on you. We’ll also start leucovorin rescue 24 hours after the infusion to help protect your body."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. Will I need blood tests during this stay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll check your methotrexate levels daily to make sure they’re going down properly. We also need to monitor your kidneys and blood counts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. And my diabetes—should I keep taking metformin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:10:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll hold metformin while you’re here because of the chemotherapy. Your sugars will be checked regularly, and you can restart it when you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my ostomy—lately I’ve had more output and some belly pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We tested a stool sample, and it came back positive for C. diff. That’s likely causing the symptoms. We’ve started you on oral vancomycin to treat it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I had that before. Is it dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be, especially with your immune system being low, but we caught it early. The treatment should clear it up in a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’m also on pentamidine monthly—is that happening this stay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:20:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s scheduled for tomorrow. It’s to prevent lung infections due to your immune deficiency."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Last time I had some trouble breathing after it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:23:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor you closely. If you have any wheezing, we can give albuterol right away. We’ll also give pre-medications to reduce the risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2152-03-17 16:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, that makes me feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2152-03-17 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re about to start your methotrexate infusion. It’ll take a few hours. A nurse will be with you the whole time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2152-03-17 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. Any side effects I should watch for now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2152-03-17 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nausea or headache are possible. Let us know right away if you feel short of breath, dizzy, or have a rash."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2152-03-17 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m feeling a bit nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2152-03-17 20:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you some ondansetron to help with that. Drink small sips of water if you can."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2152-03-18 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your methotrexate level is 0.50, which is where we expect it. Your kidneys are handling it well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2152-03-18 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I feel okay—just a little tired."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2152-03-18 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give your IVIG today to support your immune system. It’s part of your regular treatment for common variable immune deficiency."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2152-03-18 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, every three weeks. Does it help prevent infections?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2152-03-18 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it gives your body the antibodies it can’t make on its own. It’s important with your lymphoma and chemotherapy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2152-03-18 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "After the pentamidine, I started wheezing a bit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2152-03-18 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We gave you an albuterol nebulizer, and your breathing improved. No oxygen was needed. It’s a known reaction, but we’ll watch you closely next time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2152-03-18 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’m glad it passed quickly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2152-03-19 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your methotrexate level is now 0.04, and it should drop to undetectable by tomorrow. That means the leucovorin is working well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2152-03-19 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Does that mean I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2152-03-19 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly tomorrow, if everything stays on track. We’ll check one more level to confirm it’s cleared."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2152-03-19 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my back pain—it’s been flaring up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2152-03-19 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can adjust your methadone or add cyclobenzaprine if needed. Let’s try an extra dose now and see how you feel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2152-03-19 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The pain’s better now, thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2152-03-19 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We also stopped your levofloxacin. It’s no longer needed, and we want to avoid unnecessary antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2152-03-19 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And the vancomycin for C. diff—how long will I take that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2152-03-19 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll finish a 10-day course at home. We’ll send it with you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2152-03-20 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest methotrexate level is undetectable. That’s excellent. We can plan for discharge tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2152-03-20 06:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2152-03-20 06:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take leucovorin for one more day—two tablets every six hours for five doses. Continue the vancomycin, and restart metformin as directed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2152-03-20 06:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds—everything else stays the same?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2152-03-20 06:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, except we’re changing your dronabinol dose to 2.5 mg twice a day. It should help with nausea and appetite without making you too drowsy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2152-03-20 06:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll watch how I feel on that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2152-03-20 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve scheduled your next methotrexate cycle in a few weeks. Your oncologist will confirm the date."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2152-03-20 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my IVIG—same schedule?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2152-03-20 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, three weeks from your last dose. Your infusion center will contact you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2152-03-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’ll discharge you in a couple of hours. A nurse will review your medications and home instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2152-03-21 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I’m glad this round went smoothly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2152-03-21 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. Keep monitoring your ostomy and call if you have fever, severe pain, or breathing trouble. Otherwise, see you at your next appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2152-03-21 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for taking such good care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2152-03-21 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care and rest well at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2152-03-21 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing—should I watch for mouth sores this time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2152-03-21 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The lower dose makes that less likely. But if you notice any sores, start using the magic mouthwash and let your team know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2152-03-21 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my thyroid—do I need a blood test soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2152-03-21 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your levothyroxine dose is stable. Your primary doctor can check your levels at your next visit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2152-03-21 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2152-03-21 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The discharge papers are ready. You’ll take potassium supplements too—four capsules daily with food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2152-03-21 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that for my heart or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2152-03-21 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Both. Chemo and C. diff can lower potassium. This helps keep your levels safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2152-03-21 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I’ll take it with dinner."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2152-03-21 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your ostomy care again before you leave. Any final questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2152-03-21 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’m all set. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2152-03-21 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll see you for your next treatment. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2152-03-21 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, just to confirm—I take the leucovorin every six hours starting today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2152-03-21 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, two tablets every six hours for five total doses. That’s one day’s worth. It helps clear any remaining chemo from your system."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2152-03-21 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. I’ll set an alarm."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2152-03-17 15:51:00",
    "admission_end": "2152-03-21 14:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for her sixth cycle of high-dose methotrexate for primary colonic diffuse large B-cell lymphoma with CNS involvement. The chemotherapy was administered at a reduced dose of 3500 mg/m² and was well tolerated without mucositis. Leucovorin rescue was initiated 24 hours post-infusion, and methotrexate levels declined appropriately, becoming undetectable by the third day. She received IVIG for common variable immune deficiency and pentamidine for PJP prophylaxis, though she experienced transient shortness of breath after pentamidine that resolved with albuterol. A concurrent C. difficile infection was diagnosed and treated with oral vancomycin. Her diabetes was managed by holding metformin during admission, and she was discharged home with medication adjustments and close follow-up. She remained stable throughout the stay and was discharged in good condition.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Other malignant lymphomas, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Sciatica",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism"
    ]
  }
}
